# Security Group Documentation

## Domain Information

**Domain Name:** NMG.com

## Organizational Units (OUs)

The following Organizational Units (OUs) were created to organize users by department:

- Finance
- Human Resources (HR)
- Information Technology (IT)
- Operations

## Security Groups

The following Active Directory security groups were created to implement Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):

| Security Group | Purpose |

| Finance-Users | Grants Finance employees access to finance-related resources and shared folders. |
| HR-Users | Grants Human Resources staff access to employee records, onboarding documentation, and HR resources. |
| IT-Users | Grants IT personnel administrative access to Active Directory, workstations, laptops, and other IT management tools. |
| Operations-Users | Grants Operations staff access to scheduling, inventory management, and operational reports. |

## RBAC Design

Each department is assigned a dedicated security group. User permissions are granted through group membership rather than assigning permissions directly to individual accounts.

This approach:

- Simplifies permission management
- Supports the Principle of Least Privilege
- Improves scalability as the organization grows
- Reduces administrative overhead
- Makes auditing user permissions easier
